      <h3>Recovery Point Objective (RPO):</h3>
      <p> 99minds has configured its infrastructure to provide one hour or less of data loss. This is calculated from the point of the disruption, and not from 99minds’s disaster declaration.99minds would continually review the business continuity program based on lessons learned from actual events, exercises, and audits. This includes updating BCPs, refining response procedures, and enhancing training and awareness efforts.</p>
      <h3>Business Impact Analysis</h3>
      <p>Business Impact Assessment (BIA) is carried out for all applicable processes that form the basis for BCP & DRP. All critical operations, processes, and facilities are included as part of BIA, and accordingly, BCP and DRP requirements are planned. Dependencies are identified and all applicable strategies have been considered as part of BCP and DRP requirements.</p>
      <h3>Crisis Management</h3>
      <p>99minds had established a Crisis Management Team (CMT) responsible for coordinating response efforts during emergencies. The CMT will be composed of senior leaders from key functional areas and will be tasked with decision-making, communication, and resource allocation during crises.</p>
      <h3>ICT Readiness</h3>
      <p>99minds is dedicated to ensuring the resilience of its ICT services by maintaining an organizational structure equipped to prepare for and respond to disruptions, regularly evaluating and approving continuity plans aligned with business objectives, and outlining comprehensive performance, recovery time, and recovery point objectives.</p>
      <h3>Real-Time Back-Up</h3>
      <p>All data hosted on the cloud is synced in real-time (with cross-regional network latency) across the AZs (Availability Zones) or to a separate AWS region other than the one that hosts Customer serving infrastructure. Each AWS  region is designed to be completely isolated from the AWS regions & hence helps achieve the greatest possible fault tolerance and stability. Data sync happens in the active-active model and is equipped to independently handle the load in case of any failures. Backup and restore testing are conducted on an annual basis for ensuring the integrity of backup and effectiveness of restore processes within the organization.</p>
      <h3>Fault Tolerance Using High Availability & Redundancy</h3>
      <p>99minds uses high-availability solutions to provide continuous service to its Customers. 99minds provides highly available/ high availability (HA) services using AWS and Azure Availability Zones (AZ) within the AWS and Azure region in which 99minds hosts the application for the Customers. Each AWS and 99minds place resources and data in multiple of these locations within the region. Each AZ is physically separated within a metropolitan region, connected through low latency links, located in lower-risk flood plains, and supported by different grids for power supply and multiple tier-1 transit providers, UPS, and on-site backup generators, reducing Single Points of Failure (SPOF).</p>
